\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\tag{ftip}
\tag{feedback}
\tag{measurability}

\card{Remark}{How we formulate non-anticipating feedback}{
\p{We formulate online measurability to separate the index attached to a label
from the information used to produce it. The process-supervision construction
in \citet{Section 2.6}{lightman2023verify} supplies step-indexed training
labels, but it does not require every such label to be available while the
response is being generated.}

\p{This distinction determines which interventions are admissible. An online
agent may act on currently measurable feedback; an offline learner may use a
post-hoc label for a past prefix; a causal claim needs assumptions connecting
either signal to the consequences of the earlier action.}
}
